WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.823
Week 19: Imperfect: Background and Habit. describe how things used to be set a scene contrast past and present

2
00:00:07.823 --> 00:00:15.071
Cultural lens. Memory, nostalgia, and generational change without assuming one shared experience.

3
00:00:15.071 --> 00:00:27.249
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:27.249 --> 00:00:39.277
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:39.277 --> 00:00:48.298
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:48.298 --> 00:01:15.409
Model language. Antes había menos edificios. — There used to be fewer buildings. De niña jugaba en esta plaza. — As a girl, I used to play in this plaza. Eran las ocho y llovía mucho. — It was eight o'clock and raining heavily. Mientras trabajábamos, escuchábamos la radio. — While we worked, we listened to the radio. La ciudad parecía más tranquila. — The city seemed quieter.

7
00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:25.414
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
